SUMMARY:Morning Book Club
DESCRIPTION:October 15 My Grandmother Asked Me to Tell You She’s Sorry by 
 Fredrik Backman\n\nElsa is seven years old and different. Her grandmother 
 is seventy-seven years old and crazy—as in 
 standing-on-the-balcony-firing-paintball-guns-at-strangers crazy. She is 
 also Elsa’s best\, and only\, friend. At night Elsa takes refuge in her 
 grandmother’s stories\, where everybody is different and nobody needs to 
 be normal.\n\nWhen Elsa’s grandmother dies and leaves behind a series of 
 letters apologizing to people she has wronged\, Elsa’s greatest adventure 
 begins. Her grandmother’s instructions lead her to an apartment building 
 full of drunks\, monsters\, attack dogs\, and old crones but also to the 
 truth about fairy tales\, kingdoms & a grandmother like no other.
LOCATION:West Caldwell - New Book Area
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10340-17032140
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17032140
